  "verbalization": "Carvedilol is proposed to be associated with Hypertension through a mechanism involving hypovolemia, a side effect that indirectly links to the condition. The evidence suggests that Carvedilol may cause hypovolemia, which in turn is linked to Indapamide and Nifedipine, both of which are indicated for Hypertension. This creates a chain of effects where Carvedilol's side effect of hypovolemia could contribute to the development of hypertension in some individuals. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Carvedilol to Hypertension through hypovolemia supports a mechanistic link, though the exact role of hypovolemia in this context remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Carvedilol to influence blood pressure through a side effect that is not directly pharmacologically targeted.",
